The core codebase of Quantum Torsion Folder (QTF) was originally developed by the authors and is distributed under the MIT License in the main branch of this repository.

However, this specific branch of the QTF repository contains code that directly integrates and depends on PyRosetta. Because PyRosetta is not distributed under the MIT License, the software in this branch is governed by the PyRosetta licensing terms to ensure full legal compliance.

PYROSETTA LICENSING TERMS:
Academic and commercial licensing of PyRosetta is handled with a license similar to the standard Rosetta license through Rosetta Commons. 

- Academic and Non-Profit Use: Licensing is free for academic and non-profit institutions.
- Commercial Use: Licensing is available to commercial users for a fee. 

By using, copying, or distributing the code in this branch, you agree to comply with the Rosetta Commons licensing terms. For more information on obtaining the appropriate license for PyRosetta, please visit the Rosetta Commons licensing page (https://els2.comotion.uw.edu/product/rosetta).

If you require the fully open-source, MIT-licensed version of QTF that does not include the PyRosetta integration, please use the `main` branch of this repository.
